        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 74-year-old female patient, admitted on 24/08/2023 with an acute exacerbation of known COPD. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Physical examination revealed prolonged expiration and bilateral wheeze. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. She was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), and a course of systemic corticosteroids. Oxygen saturation was continuously monitored throughout the stay. She improved satisfactorily and was discharged on 25/08/2023. Please ensure continuation of her inhaler regimen and arrange early follow-up. Pulmonary rehabilitation referral is recommended. Kind regards, Dr. [Treating Physician], Department of Internal Medicine.</div>"
            },
